"answer": "Warning signs of mental disorders in older adults involving mood, sleep, withdrawal, or self-harm thoughts include: changes in mood or energy level; changes in sleeping habits; withdrawing from people and activities enjoyed; feeling unusually confused, angry, upset, worried, or scared; feeling numb or like nothing matters; feeling sadness or hopelessness; and thinking of harming yourself or others [MLP-7427]. Additionally, specific suicide warning signs relevant to older adults include talking about wanting to die, feeling empty or hopeless, sleeping too little or too much, withdrawing from family or friends, and displaying extreme mood swings [MLP-424]."
}
